{"task_id": "HumanEval/12", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Optional\n\n\ndef longest(strings: List[str]) -> Optional[str]:\n    \"\"\"Returns the longest string from a list, or `None` if the list is empty.\n    If multiple strings share the maximum length, the first one encountered is returned.\"\"\"\n    if not strings:\n        return None\n\n    # Initialize longest_str to None and max_length to -1.\n    # This ensures the first string encountered will always be set as the initial longest.\n    longest_str: Optional[str] = None\n    max_length: int = -1\n\n    for s in strings:\n        # Update if the current string is longer, or if it's the first string being processed.\n        # This condition naturally handles ties by keeping the existing longest_str\n        # if the current string has an equal length.\n        if longest_str is None or len(s) > max_length:\n            longest_str = s\n            max_length = len(s)\n\n    return longest_str\n```"}
