{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "def fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Computes the n-th element of the Fib4 number sequence iteratively.\n    This function avoids recursion for efficiency.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 2\n    if n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize a list to store sequence values for dynamic programming.\n    # The size n+1 accommodates indices from 0 to n.\n    dp = [0] * (n + 1)\n    dp[0] = 0\n    dp[1] = 0\n    dp[2] = 2\n    dp[3] = 0\n\n    for i in range(4, n + 1):\n        dp[i] = dp[i-1] + dp[i-2] + dp[i-3] + dp[i-4]\n\n    return dp[n]"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "```python\ndef fib4(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Computes the n-th element of the Fib4 number sequence iteratively.\n    The sequence is defined by specific base cases and a sum of the four preceding terms.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 2\n    if n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize with the first four values: fib4(0), fib4(1), fib4(2), fib4(3)\n    fib4_values = [0, 0, 2, 0]\n\n    for _ in range(4, n + 1):\n        next_fib4 = sum(fib4_values)\n        # Shift values: remove the oldest and add the newest.\n        fib4_values.pop(0)\n        fib4_values.append(next_fib4)\n\n    return fib4_values[3]\n```"}
