{"task_id": "HumanEval/65", "solution": "def circular_shift(x, shift):\n    \"\"\"Circular shift digits of x right by 'shift', returning a string. If 'shift' exceeds digit count, digits are reversed.\"\"\"\n    x_str = str(x)\n    \n    sign = ''\n    if x_str.startswith('-'):\n        sign = '-'\n        x_str = x_str[1:]\n\n    num_digits = len(x_str)\n\n    if shift > num_digits:\n        shifted_str = x_str[::-1]\n    else:\n        effective_shift = shift % num_digits\n        shifted_str = x_str[-effective_shift:] + x_str[:-effective_shift]\n    \n    return sign + shifted_str"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/63", "solution": "```python\n_memo = {}\n\ndef fibfib(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Efficiently computes the n-th element of the FibFib number sequence.\n    The sequence is defined by fibfib(0)=0, fibfib(1)=0, fibfib(2)=1, and fibfib(n) = fibfib(n-1) + fibfib(n-2) + fibfib(n-3) for n > 2.\n    >>> fibfib(1)\n    0\n    >>> fibfib(5)\n    4\n    >>> fibfib(8)\n    24\n    \"\"\"\n    if n in _memo:\n        return _memo[n]\n\n    if n == 0:\n        result = 0\n    elif n == 1:\n        result = 0\n    elif n == 2:\n        result = 1\n    else:\n        result = fibfib(n - 1) + fibfib(n - 2) + fibfib(n - 3)\n\n    _memo[n] = result\n    return result\n```"}
