{"task_id": "HumanEval/76", "solution": "def is_simple_power(x, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if x is a simple power of n (n^k = x for non-negative integer k).\n    Assumes integer inputs for x and n.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Handle special cases for n, following FR1.1 and FR1.2\n    if n == 1:\n        return x == 1\n    if n == 0:\n        return x == 0\n\n    # Handle negative inputs for x or n, following FR1.5 and FR1.6\n    if x < 0 or n < 0:\n        return False\n    \n    # Handle x = 0 (and n is not 0 or 1), following FR1.3\n    if x == 0:\n        return False\n\n    # At this point: x > 0 and n > 1.\n    # The case x=1 and n>1 (e.g., is_simple_power(1, 4)) implies n^0 = 1.\n    # The loop condition `temp_x > 1` will correctly handle this, making the loop not run\n    # and `return temp_x == 1` yield true.\n\n    # Repeatedly divide x by n, following FR1.7, FR1.8, FR1.9\n    temp_x = x\n    while temp_x % n == 0 and temp_x > 1:\n        temp_x //= n\n    return temp_x == 1"}
