{"task_id": "HumanEval/86", "solution": "import re\n\ndef anti_shuffle(s):\n    \"\"\"\n    Takes a string and returns an ordered version of it.\n    Words are replaced by a new word where characters are arranged in ascending ASCII order.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not s:\n        return s\n\n    # Helper function to sort characters within a word, inline.\n    def _sort_word_characters(word_str: str) -> str:\n        return \"\".join(sorted(word_str))\n\n    # Split the string by sequences of spaces, keeping the spaces as tokens.\n    tokens = re.split(r'(\\s+)', s)\n\n    processed_tokens = []\n    for token in tokens:\n        # If the token is not purely whitespace (it's a word), sort its characters.\n        if token.strip():\n            processed_tokens.append(_sort_word_characters(token))\n        else: # It's a sequence of spaces or an empty string from the split\n            processed_tokens.append(token)\n    \n    return \"\".join(processed_tokens)"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/89", "solution": "```python\ndef encrypt(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Encrypts a string by rotating alphabetic characters by a fixed shift.\n    Non-alphabetic characters remain unchanged, and case is preserved.\"\"\"\n    ROTATION_SHIFT = 4\n    encrypted_chars = []\n\n    for char in s:\n        # Check if the character is an English alphabet letter (a-z or A-Z)\n        is_alphabetic = ('a' <= char <= 'z' or 'A' <= char <= 'Z')\n\n        if is_alphabetic:\n            # Determine the starting ordinal for the respective case (lowercase 'a' or uppercase 'A')\n            start_ord = ord('a') if 'a' <= char <= 'z' else ord('A')\n            # Calculate the new ordinal, applying the shift and handling alphabet wrap-around\n            rotated_ord = start_ord + (ord(char) - start_ord + ROTATION_SHIFT) % 26\n            encrypted_chars.append(chr(rotated_ord))\n        else:\n            # Non-alphabetic characters are appended without modification\n            encrypted_chars.append(char)\n\n    return \"\".join(encrypted_chars)\n```"}
