{"task_id": "HumanEval/99", "solution": "import math\n\ndef closest_integer(value):\n    '''\n    Returns the closest integer to a numeric string, rounding away from zero for equidistant values.\n    Handles both positive and negative numbers with decimals.\n    '''\n    number = float(value)\n\n    if number == int(number):\n        return int(number)\n\n    floor_val = math.floor(number)\n    ceil_val = math.ceil(number)\n\n    dist_to_floor = abs(number - floor_val)\n    dist_to_ceil = abs(number - ceil_val)\n\n    if dist_to_floor == dist_to_ceil: # Equidistant (e.g., X.5)\n        if number > 0:\n            return int(ceil_val) # Round up for positive (away from zero)\n        else:\n            return int(floor_val) # Round down for negative (away from zero)\n    elif dist_to_floor < dist_to_ceil:\n        return int(floor_val)\n    else:\n        return int(ceil_val)"}
