{"task_id": "HumanEval/99", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef closest_integer(value):\n    '''\n    Returns the closest integer to a number represented as a string.\n    Equidistant numbers (X.5) are rounded away from zero.\n    '''\n    num = float(value)\n\n    floor_num = math.floor(num)\n    ceil_num = math.ceil(num)\n\n    # If the number has exactly a 0.5 fractional part, round it away from zero.\n    if num - floor_num == 0.5:\n        return int(ceil_num) if num > 0 else int(floor_num)\n    else:\n        # Otherwise, round to the nearest integer.\n        if abs(num - floor_num) < abs(num - ceil_num):\n            return int(floor_num)\n        else:\n            return int(ceil_num)\n```"}
