{"task_id": "HumanEval/112", "solution": "def reverse_delete(s, c):\n    \"\"\"Deletes characters from s that are in c, then checks if the resulting string is a palindrome.\n    Returns a tuple containing the modified string and the palindrome check result.\"\"\"\n    \n    chars_to_delete_set = set(c)\n    modified_s = \"\".join(char for char in s if char not in chars_to_delete_set)\n    \n    is_palindrome = modified_s == modified_s[::-1]\n    \n    return (modified_s, is_palindrome)"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/112", "solution": "```python\ndef reverse_delete(s, c):\n    \"\"\"\n    Deletes characters from s present in c, then checks if the resulting string is a palindrome.\n    Returns a tuple of the modified string and the palindrome check result.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Helper function to remove characters\n    def _remove_chars(input_s: str, chars_to_remove_str: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Removes all characters from input_s that are present in chars_to_remove_str.\"\"\"\n        result = []\n        chars_set = set(chars_to_remove_str)\n        for char_s in input_s:\n            if char_s not in chars_set:\n                result.append(char_s)\n        return \"\".join(result)\n\n    # Helper function to check for palindrome\n    def _is_palindrome(input_s: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a string is a palindrome.\"\"\"\n        return input_s == input_s[::-1]\n\n    modified_s = _remove_chars(s, c)\n    is_palindrome = _is_palindrome(modified_s)\n    return (modified_s, is_palindrome)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/113", "solution": "def odd_count(lst):\n    \"\"\"Analyzes a list of digit strings, returning a list of formatted strings. Each output string describes the count of odd digits in the corresponding input string.\"\"\"\n    OUTPUT_TEMPLATE = \"the number of odd elements {count}n the str{count}ng {count} of the {count}nput.\"\n    results = []\n    for s in lst:\n        odd_digit_count = 0\n        for char_digit in s:\n            digit = int(char_digit)\n            if digit % 2 != 0:\n                odd_digit_count += 1\n        \n        formatted_string = OUTPUT_TEMPLATE.format(count=odd_digit_count)\n        results.append(formatted_string)\n    return results"}
