{"task_id": "HumanEval/118", "solution": "```python\ndef get_closest_vowel(word):\n    \"\"\"Finds the rightmost vowel in a word strictly surrounded by two consonants.\n    Returns an empty string if no such vowel is found or the word is too short.\n    \"\"\"\n    VOWELS = \"aeiouAEIOU\"\n\n    def is_vowel(char: str) -> bool:\n        # Checks if a character is an English vowel, case-sensitive.\n        return char in VOWELS\n\n    def is_consonant(char: str) -> bool:\n        # Checks if a character is an English consonant, case-sensitive.\n        # Assumes the input character is an English letter.\n        return not is_vowel(char)\n\n    if len(word) < 3:\n        return \"\"\n\n    # Iterate from right to left, excluding the first and last characters.\n    # The valid range for 'i' is from len(word) - 2 down to 1 (inclusive).\n    for i in range(len(word) - 2, 0, -1):\n        current_char = word[i]\n        if is_vowel(current_char):\n            left_char = word[i - 1]\n            right_char = word[i + 1]\n            if is_consonant(left_char) and is_consonant(right_char):\n                return current_char\n    return \"\"\n```"}
