{"task_id": "HumanEval/150", "solution": "def x_or_y(n, x, y):\n    \"\"\"A simple program which should return the value of x if n is \n    a prime number and should return the value of y otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _is_prime(num):\n        \"\"\"Checks if a given number is prime using an optimized trial division.\"\"\"\n        if num <= 1:\n            return False\n        if num <= 3:\n            return True\n        if num % 2 == 0 or num % 3 == 0:\n            return False\n        i = 5\n        while i * i <= num:\n            if num % i == 0 or num % (i + 2) == 0:\n                return False\n            i += 6\n        return True\n\n    if _is_prime(n):\n        return x\n    else:\n        return y"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/147", "solution": "```python\ndef get_max_triples(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts triples (a[i], a[j], a[k]) from a generated array 'a' where i < j < k,\n    and a[i] + a[j] + a[k] is a multiple of 3. Array elements a[i] = i*i - i + 1.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _nCr(n_val, r_val):\n        \"\"\"Calculates 'n choose r' (binomial coefficient). Returns 0 if n < r or r < 0.\"\"\"\n        if r_val < 0 or r_val > n_val:\n            return 0\n        if r_val == 0 or r_val == n_val:\n            return 1\n        if r_val > n_val // 2:\n            r_val = n_val - r_val\n        \n        res = 1\n        for i in range(r_val):\n            res = res * (n_val - i) // (i + 1)\n        return res\n\n    # If n is too small to form a triple (i.e., n < 3), the count is 0.\n    if n < 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # Analyze a[x] = x*x - x + 1 modulo 3.\n    # a[x] % 3 is 0 if x % 3 is 2. Otherwise, a[x] % 3 is 1.\n    count_rem0 = 0\n    count_rem1 = 0\n\n    for x_val in range(1, n + 1):\n        if x_val % 3 == 2:\n            count_rem0 += 1\n        else: # x_val % 3 == 0 or x_val % 3 == 1\n            count_rem1 += 1\n\n    # A sum of three numbers is a multiple of 3 if all three have remainder 0,\n    # or all three have remainder 1, when divided by 3.\n    total_triples = _nCr(count_rem0, 3) + _nCr(count_rem1, 3)\n    \n    return total_triples\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/148", "solution": "PLANET_NAMES_ORDERED = [\n    \"Mercury\", \"Venus\", \"Earth\", \"Mars\", \"Jupiter\", \"Saturn\", \"Uranus\", \"Neptune\"\n]\n\nPLANET_ORDER_MAP = {name: i + 1 for i, name in enumerate(PLANET_NAMES_ORDERED)}\n\ndef bf(planet1, planet2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns planets between planet1 and planet2, sorted by proximity to the Sun.\n    Returns an empty tuple if any input planet name is invalid.\n    \"\"\"\n    order1 = PLANET_ORDER_MAP.get(planet1)\n    order2 = PLANET_ORDER_MAP.get(planet2)\n\n    if order1 is None or order2 is None:\n        return ()\n\n    min_order = min(order1, order2)\n    max_order = max(order1, order2)\n\n    intermediate_planets = []\n    for i, planet_name in enumerate(PLANET_NAMES_ORDERED):\n        current_planet_order = i + 1\n        if min_order < current_planet_order < max_order:\n            intermediate_planets.append(planet_name)\n            \n    return tuple(intermediate_planets)"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/150", "solution": "import math\n\ndef x_or_y(n, x, y):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns x if n is a prime number, otherwise returns y.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _is_prime(num: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Determines if a given integer is a prime number.\"\"\"\n        if num <= 1:\n            return False\n        if num == 2:\n            return True\n        if num % 2 == 0:\n            return False\n        for i in range(3, int(math.sqrt(num)) + 1, 2):\n            if num % i == 0:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    if _is_prime(n):\n        return x\n    else:\n        return y"}
