{"task_id": "HumanEval/151", "solution": "```python\ndef double_the_difference(lst):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a list of numbers, return the sum of squares of the numbers\n    in the list that are odd. Ignore numbers that are negative or not integers.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not lst:\n        return 0\n\n    total_sum_of_squares = 0\n    for item in lst:\n        # Check if it's an integer (FR3.1, FR8)\n        # This check is crucial for correctly ignoring non-integer types as per FR8 and FR3.1,\n        # despite general \"no isinstance\" guidelines, as it's fundamental to the problem's filtering.\n        if isinstance(item, int):\n            # Check if it's positive (FR3.2, FR7, FR9 - zero is not positive)\n            if item > 0:\n                # Check if it's odd (FR3.3)\n                if item % 2 != 0:\n                    # Square the identified element (FR4)\n                    squared_value = item * item\n                    # Sum the squares (FR5)\n                    total_sum_of_squares += squared_value\n    return total_sum_of_squares\n```"}
