{"task_id": "HumanEval/158", "solution": "```python\ndef find_max(words):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the word with the maximum number of unique characters.\n    If tied, the word that comes first lexicographically is returned.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not words:\n        return \"\"\n\n    max_unique_count = -1\n    result_word = \"\"\n\n    for word in words:\n        current_unique_count = len(set(word))\n\n        if current_unique_count > max_unique_count:\n            max_unique_count = current_unique_count\n            result_word = word\n        elif current_unique_count == max_unique_count:\n            # Apply lexicographical tie-breaker\n            if word < result_word:\n                result_word = word\n    return result_word\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/160", "solution": "```python\ndef do_algebra(operator, operand):\n    \"\"\"\n    Constructs and evaluates an algebraic expression from given operators and operands.\n    The function trusts inputs are valid according to the problem description.\n    \"\"\"\n    expression_parts = []\n    for i in range(len(operand)):\n        expression_parts.append(str(operand[i]))\n        if i < len(operator):\n            expression_parts.append(operator[i])\n\n    expression = \" \".join(expression_parts)\n    result = eval(expression)\n    return int(result)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/160", "solution": "def do_algebra(operator, operand):\n    \"\"\"\n    Constructs and evaluates an algebraic expression from a list of operators and operands.\n    The result follows standard mathematical precedence.\n    \"\"\"\n    expression_parts = []\n    for i in range(len(operator)):\n        expression_parts.append(str(operand[i]))\n        expression_parts.append(operator[i])\n    expression_parts.append(str(operand[-1]))\n\n    expression_str = \" \".join(expression_parts)\n    return int(eval(expression_str))"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/161", "solution": "def solve(s):\n    \"\"\"\n    Transforms a string: reverses case of letters, or reverses the whole string\n    if no letters are present.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Determine if the string contains any alphabetic characters.\n    contains_letters = any(char.isalpha() for char in s)\n\n    if not contains_letters:\n        # If no letters, reverse the entire string.\n        return s[::-1]\n    else:\n        # If letters are present, iterate and reverse case of letters; non-letters remain unchanged.\n        transformed_chars = []\n        for char in s:\n            transformed_chars.append(char.swapcase())\n        return \"\".join(transformed_chars)"}
