{"task_id": "HumanEval/162", "solution": "```python\nimport hashlib\nfrom typing import Optional\n\ndef string_to_md5(text: str) -> Optional[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a string 'text', return its MD5 hash equivalent.\n    Returns None if 'text' is an empty string.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not text:\n        return None\n    # Compute the MD5 hash of the UTF-8 encoded string and return its hexadecimal digest.\n    return hashlib.md5(text.encode('utf-8')).hexdigest()\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/162", "solution": "```python\nimport hashlib\n\ndef string_to_md5(text):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a string 'text', return its md5 hash equivalent string.\n    If 'text' is an empty string, return None.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not text:\n        return None\n    # Encode the string to bytes using UTF-8 and compute its MD5 hash.\n    return hashlib.md5(text.encode('utf-8')).hexdigest()\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/163", "solution": "def generate_integers(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given two positive integers a and b, return the even integers between a\n    and b, in ascending order.\n    Handles cases where a > b and returns an empty list if no even numbers are found.\n    \"\"\"\n    min_val = min(a, b)\n    max_val = max(a, b)\n\n    even_numbers = []\n    # Start from the first even number greater than or equal to min_val\n    start = min_val if min_val % 2 == 0 else min_val + 1\n\n    for i in range(start, max_val + 1, 2):\n        even_numbers.append(i)\n\n    return even_numbers"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/163", "solution": "EVEN_DIGITS = [0, 2, 4, 6, 8]\n\ndef generate_integers(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given two positive integers a and b, return the even digits (0, 2, 4, 6, 8)\n    between a and b (inclusive), in ascending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    min_val = min(a, b)\n    max_val = max(a, b)\n\n    result = []\n    for digit in EVEN_DIGITS:\n        if min_val <= digit <= max_val:\n            result.append(digit)\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/161", "solution": "def solve(s):\n    \"\"\"Processes a string: reverses letter cases or reverses the entire string if no letters are present.\n    Non-letter characters remain unchanged unless the entire string is reversed.\n    \"\"\"\n    has_letters_in_string = False\n    for char in s:\n        if char.isalpha():\n            has_letters_in_string = True\n            break\n\n    if not has_letters_in_string:\n        # If no letters are present, reverse the entire string.\n        return s[::-1]\n    else:\n        # If letters are present, iterate and reverse case for letters.\n        result_chars = []\n        for char in s:\n            if char.isalpha():\n                if char.islower():\n                    result_chars.append(char.upper())\n                elif char.isupper():\n                    result_chars.append(char.lower())\n                else:\n                    # Handles cases where isalpha() is true but neither islower() nor isupper() (e.g., titlecase, or non-ASCII letters without clear upper/lower distinction).\n                    result_chars.append(char)\n            else:\n                result_chars.append(char)\n        return \"\".join(result_chars)"}
